        "paragraphs": [
            "The Command family is Cohere's family of text-generation large language models. Cohere says they power tool-using agents, retrieval augmented generation (RAG), translation, copywriting, and similar use cases, and that they work through the Chat endpoint, which can be used with or without RAG. The family includes Command A+, Command A, Command A Translate, Command A Vision, Command R, and Command R7B. Command is Cohere's default generation model that takes a user instruction and generates text following the instruction, and Cohere says the models also have conversational capabilities, making them well-suited for chat applications.",
            "Cohere describes Command A+ as an open-source enterprise workhorse built for complex reasoning, multimodal and multilingual agentic tasks, released under an Apache 2.0 license. Cohere says Command A+ is a mixture-of-experts model with 218B total and 25B active parameters, a 128K input context and 64K maximum generation, and support for 48 languages. Command R+ and Command R are large language models optimized for conversational interaction and long-context tasks, with a 128,000-token context window and a maximum of 4,000 output tokens. Command R7B is the smallest and fastest model in the R family, with a 128K context window.",
            "Cohere offers the Command models on its proprietary platform, Microsoft Azure, and Oracle GenAI Service. Command A+ is available on Hugging Face and can be deployed in Model Vault, and Command R7B is available on the Cohere Platform and Hugging Face."
        ],
